{%- doc -%}
  Outputs the display-only estimate of the "Elite member 5% OFF" automatic
  discount, in cents (integer, e.g. `349`), or `0` when it should not be shown.

  Why this exists: the real discount is an order-discount Shopify Function
  (target purchase.order-discount.run) that only evaluates at checkout, so it
  doesn't appear in the cart until the customer has been through checkout once.
  This mirrors the function's eligibility purely for display; the actual discount
  still applies at checkout regardless of what we render.

  Single source of truth for the estimate — used by both cart summaries. Because
  `render` runs in an isolated scope, capture the output in the caller:

    {%- capture elite_estimated_savings -%}{%- render 'elite-discount-estimate' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign elite_estimated_savings = elite_estimated_savings | plus: 0 -%}

  Eligibility mirrors src/run.ts of the discount function:
    - customer is Elite (tag inveterate-tier#99a431e2 / #dc38b982, or a
      "Membership" line in the cart), and
    - NOT tagged 'inveterate-cancelled', and
    - 5% off the order subtotal EXCLUDING the excluded variant ids.
  Returns 0 when the real discount is already applied (avoids double-display).

  Rounding: Shopify applies the discount with allocation_method "across" and
  floors each line's allocation to the cent, so we sum the per-line floored 5%
  (`line | times: 5 | divided_by: 100`, integer division = floor). Flooring the
  whole subtotal instead would overshoot the real discount by a few cents on
  multi-line carts.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign elite_excluded_variants = ',41861249073249,41861249106017,41861249138785,41861249171553,41861249204321,41711861792865,'
  assign elite_estimated_savings = 0
  assign elite_is_elite = false
  assign elite_is_cancelled = false

  for tag in customer.tags
    if tag == 'inveterate-tier#99a431e2' or tag == 'inveterate-tier#dc38b982'
      assign elite_is_elite = true
    elsif tag == 'inveterate-cancelled'
      assign elite_is_cancelled = true
    endif
  endfor

  unless elite_is_elite
    for item in cart.items
      if item.title contains 'Membership'
        assign elite_is_elite = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endunless

  assign elite_discount_already_applied = false
  for discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications
    if discount.title contains 'Elite member'
      assign elite_discount_already_applied = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  if elite_is_elite and elite_is_cancelled == false and elite_discount_already_applied == false
    for item in cart.items
      assign elite_variant_key = ',' | append: item.variant_id | append: ','
      unless elite_excluded_variants contains elite_variant_key
        assign elite_line_savings = item.final_line_price | times: 5 | divided_by: 100
        assign elite_estimated_savings = elite_estimated_savings | plus: elite_line_savings
      endunless
    endfor
  endif

  echo elite_estimated_savings
-%}
